data.content:
In .NET 10 MAUI, `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was removed because Android deprecated `adjustResize`. The replacement is **Edge-to-Edge mode** with proper keyboard inset handling.

**Solution:**

1. In your `MainActivity.cs`, ensure edge-to-edge is enabled (it's the default in .NET 10):

```csharp
[Activity(Theme = "@style/Maui.MainTheme", 
          WindowSoftInputMode = SoftInput.AdjustResize)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity { }
```

2. Wrap your chat page content in a layout that respects keyboard insets. In your page XAML:

```xml
<Grid>
    <Grid.RowDefinitions>
        <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
    </Grid.RowDefinitions>

    <CollectionView Grid.Row="0" ItemsSource="{Binding Messages}" />

    <Entry Grid.Row="1" 
           Placeholder="Type a message..."
           Margin="8" />
</Grid>
```

3. In `MauiProgram.cs`, configure Android to handle insets properly:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
    events.AddAndroid(android =>
    {
        android.OnCreate((activity, _) =>
        {
            AndroidX.Core.View.WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(
                activity.Window!, false);
        });
    });
});
```

4. If the above still doesn't push up your input, add a `KeyboardAccelerators`-style handler or use the **community approach** — listen for insets in a custom handler:

```csharp
// In Platforms/Android/MainPage handler or a custom Effect
AndroidX.Core.View.ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(
    platformView, new InsetsListener());
```

**TL;DR:** Set `SoftInput.AdjustResize` on your `Activity` attribute + call `SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(window, false)`. This is the .NET 10 equivalent of the old `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` behavior.
